              "subject": "[🔴 URGENT] Pipeline Alert: Silver Data Quality Threshold Exceeded",
              "body": "<p>Hello Data Engineering Team,</p>\n<p><strong>The Retail Clickstream Pipeline was stopped at Gate 2 (Silver Layer Circuit Breaker)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Issue</strong>: The processed batch exceeded the maximum allowable limits for Data Quality. Either the Dead Letter Queue (DLQ) rate exceeded 5%, or the Bot/Anomaly rate exceeded 20%.</p>\n<p>The pipeline was automatically halted to prevent corrupted or skewed data from propagating into the Gold layer and Executive Dashboards.</p>\n<p><strong>Action Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Open the Fabric Pipeline Monitor.</li>\n  <li>Review the Output/Logs of the \"nb_gate_silver\" notebook activity for exact percentages.</li>\n  <li>Investigate the anomalous data batch before resuming.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br></p>\n<p>System Generated by Microsoft Fabric.</p>"
